Package: shortcutradio
Version: @VERSION@
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Marian Raynov <marian.raynov@gmail.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/msvdm/ShortCutRadio
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.39), libpulse0, libegl1, libgl1, libxkbcommon-x11-0,
 libxcb-cursor0, libxcb-icccm4, libxcb-keysyms1, libxcb-shape0,
 libxcb-xinerama0, libfontconfig1, libfreetype6, libdbus-1-3
Description: Radio and music player that hides in a corner of the screen
 ShortCutRadio plays internet radio and your music folders. Press a shortcut and
 a small card appears in a corner of the screen, over anything, fullscreen
 games included, showing what is playing. Change station, skip a track or
 set the volume from the keyboard; the shortcuts work only while the card
 is showing, so the rest of the time every key belongs to your other apps.
 .
 Paste a station's web page and ShortCutRadio finds its streams. Station logos
 are found by themselves. Media keys, the sound menu and a tray icon work
 too. Linux on X11.
